# Jekyll Twilight

Jekyll Twilight is the source for the Agustealo Design Studio site published at https://agustealo.github.io.

## Runtime

- Jekyll 4.4.x
- Ruby 3.1 in GitHub Actions
- Plain HTML, CSS, JavaScript, and Liquid templates
- GitHub Pages deployment through Actions

## Local development

```bash
bundle install
bundle exec jekyll serve
```

The local site is available at `http://localhost:4000`.

For a production-equivalent build:

```bash
JEKYLL_ENV=production bundle exec jekyll build --trace
```

## Project structure

```text
.github/workflows/   CI and GitHub Pages deployment
_includes/           Reusable page fragments
_layouts/            Jekyll layouts
_posts/              Blog posts
css/                 Site stylesheets
images/              Site image assets
js/                  Browser runtime
_config.yml          Site metadata and Jekyll configuration
feed.xml             Custom RSS feed
index.html           Home page content
```

`_site/` is generated output and is intentionally not committed.

## Configuration

Site identity, canonical URL, social profiles, permalink behavior, excerpt behavior, and active plugins are defined in `_config.yml`.

The dependency surface is intentionally small. Jekyll owns its transitive Sass/watch dependencies; the project directly declares only Jekyll, BigDecimal, the sitemap plugin, and the SEO tag plugin.

## Quality gate

Pull requests run the `Site Quality` workflow. It installs the locked Ruby dependencies, performs a production Jekyll build, and asserts critical generated surfaces and known regression conditions.

A successful build is required evidence before a pull request should be merged.

## Deployment

Pushes to `master` use `.github/workflows/jekyll.yml` to build the source tree and deploy the generated `_site` artifact to GitHub Pages.

